  - [38;5;153msrc/store/store.js[39m — holds the task list, exposes [38;5;153mgetState()[39m, [38;5;153mdispatch(action)[39m, [38;5;153msubscribe(fn)[39m. [1mEvery mutation goes [0m
    [1mthrough here[0m — that single funnel is the whole reason the notifications phase will be cheap.
  - [38;5;153msrc/store/persistence.js[39m — the only module that touches [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m. Serializes, deserializes, versions.
  - [38;5;153msrc/ui/[39m — render functions and DOM wiring. Reads state, dispatches actions, owns no state of its own.
  - [38;5;153msrc/main.js[39m — wiring and entry point.

  [1mThe task shape:[0m

  {
    [36mid[39m: string,            [32m// crypto.randomUUID()[39m
    [36mtitle[39m: string,
    [36mdone[39m: boolean,
    [36mcreatedAt[39m: string,     [32m// ISO 8601[39m
    [36mcompletedAt[39m: string | [34mnull[39m,
    [36mdueAt[39m: string | [34mnull[39m   [32m// ISO 8601[39m
  }

  [1mPersistence.[0m One [38;5;153mlocalStorage[39m key, [38;5;153mtasks-app/v1[39m, holding [38;5;153m{ schemaVersion: 1, tasks: [...] }[39m. The version envelope is
  there so that when sub-project 2 adds fields, we migrate rather than silently corrupt whatever is already in your
  browser. Plain JSON throughout — no [38;5;153mDate[39m objects, no class instances — which is exactly what makes the eventual move
  to a server a transport change rather than a rewrite.

  The one judgment call worth flagging: [38;5;153mdueAt[39m as a full timestamp rather than a date-only string. Date-only is simpler
  to display, but "due tomorrow" reminders need a time to fire at, and widening it later means migrating stored data.
  I'd rather carry the timestamp and render just the date when the time is midnight.
